# {{.ProjectName}}

A drag & drop UI builder, generated from the Wails `ui-builder` template.

Drag components from the palette onto the artboard, tune them in the inspector,
rearrange them in the layers panel, then save the layout or export it as a
standalone HTML page — all through native dialogs provided by the Go backend.

## Getting started

```
wails3 dev      # run with hot reload
wails3 build    # produce a production binary in bin/
```

## What's inside

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `main.go` | Creates the Wails app and the builder window |
| `layoutservice.go` | `LayoutService` — save / open layouts and export HTML via native dialogs |
| `greetservice.go` | The stock greeter from the base template; safe to delete |
| `frontend/src/components.ts` | The component registry: defaults, inspector fields and renderers |
| `frontend/src/theme.ts` | Stylesheet for the components you build (shared with the export) |
| `frontend/src/store.ts` | Document state, selection and undo/redo history |
| `frontend/src/canvas.ts` | Artboard rendering, selection and drag & drop |
| `frontend/src/palette.ts` · `inspector.ts` · `layers.ts` | The three panels |
| `frontend/src/exporter.ts` | Turns a layout into a standalone HTML page |
| `frontend/public/style.css` | The builder's own chrome (panels, toolbar, indicators) |

Layouts are plain JSON (`*.uib.json`). The builder autosaves the current design
to the browser's local storage, so closing the app never loses work.

## Adding a component

Append an entry to the `components` array in `frontend/src/components.ts`:

```ts
{
    type: 'callout', label: 'Callout', category: 'Content', icon: 'quote',
    defaults: {text: 'Heads up!'},
    fields: [{key: 'text', label: 'Text', kind: 'textarea', group: 'Content'}],
    render(node) {
        const div = document.createElement('div');
        div.className = 'ub-callout';
        div.textContent = String(node.props.text ?? '');
        return div;
    },
},
```

Add its styles to `componentStyles` in `frontend/src/theme.ts` and it will show
up in the palette, render on the canvas and be included in exports. Set
`container: true` (plus `direction`) for components that accept children.

## Keyboard shortcuts

Press `?` in the app for the full list. The essentials: `⌘Z` / `⇧⌘Z` undo and
redo, `⌘D` duplicate, `⌫` delete, `⌘S` save, `⌘O` open, `⌘E` export, `⌘P`
preview. On Windows and Linux use `Ctrl` in place of `⌘`.

